## 2026-11-05 20:14 PST -- commit d3b25ef8672aa4af3db7d4552dd6e74ce2c1dde0
- What changed: Prefixwise v2, E1-ready core. Repo created (public, MIT).
  src/prefixwise/fingerprint.py (raw+canonical+masked hashes, HMAC for short blocks),
  classifier.py (19-cause v2 taxonomy), diagnostics.py (Anthropic/OpenAI
  native diagnostics chaining, no beta header), ledger.py (SQLite, tokens
  per successful task), proxy.py (stdlib OpenAI-compatible proxy, mock mode).
- Tests: PYTHONPATH=src python3 -m pytest tests/ -q -- 22 passed in 0.64s.
- Proxy smoke test: mock mode, /health ok, first turn first_write, second
  turn none, ledger endpoint returns roll-up. Fix found by smoke test:
  a first write is recorded with 0 avoidable tokens (baseline, not waste).
- Failures/fixes: SQLite threading in proxy, volatile masking of
  alphanumeric ids, tool reserialization detection (all fixed in this commit).

## 2026-11-05 20:26 PST -- commit f1da9c4cf5c37afedfb1b24b56e020655d731c3e
- Note: this entry was written before the commit was amended to fill
  in its SHA; the SHA above is the amended (final) E1-open commit.
  This log-only fix is a separate commit, so the SHA above stays correct.
- What changed: E1-open harness (experiments/e1_open/). e1_open.py runs
  100 turns against a vLLM OpenAI-compatible server (Qwen/Qwen3-8B
  default) with KNOWN injected causes as ground truth, scores classifier
  agreement and UNKNOWN rate (pass: agreement >=95%, UNKNOWN <=10%),
  writes JSON + markdown reports to experiments/e1_open/results/.
  vllm_server.sh starts vLLM >= v0.30.0 with --enable-prefix-caching,
  --enable-prompt-tokens-details, --kv-events-config, and a served-model
  alias for MODEL_SWITCH turns. colab_e1_open.ipynb runs it on Colab
  (L4, Qwen3-8B; Qwen3-4B fallback for T4). experiments/e1_open/README.md
  documents live, mock, and Colab runs. tests/test_e1_open.py adds
  scoring unit tests (mock vLLM responses, no GPU).
  Proxy change (src/prefixwise/proxy.py): track gap_seconds per session
  and accept prefixwise_compaction_event (popped before forwarding),
  so RETRY_REPLAY and COMPACTION_REWRITE can fire through the proxy.
  Main README: new E1-open section.
- Tests: PYTHONPATH=src python3 -m pytest tests/ -q -- 28 passed in 0.81s
  (22 existing + 6 new E1-open tests).
- Proxy smoke test: e1_open.py --mock (real proxy/classifier/ledger,
  simulated vLLM cached_tokens) -- 100 turns, agreement 100.0%,
  UNKNOWN rate 0.0%, Pass YES, all 9 causes 100%. This is a harness
  smoke test only, not evidence about vLLM.
- Failures/fixes:
  * test_build_body missing base_date argument -- fixed in the test.
  * Turn builder first chained identical turns wrong: user question
    changed every turn, and turns restoring a change (tool order back,
    tool restored, system wording back, post-compaction NONE/RETRY)
    were identical to the previous turn. Fixed: question fixed per
    session; turn-aware mutations (turn 5 reversed / turn 6 restored,
    turn 7 tool removed / turn 8 restored, turn 9 system edited /
    turn 10 restored, turns 5-7 repeat the turn-4 compacted history).
    Mock agreement went from 95.0% (NONE 15/20, turn-10 NONE scored
    HISTORY_EDIT) to 100.0% after fixing the turn-10 override to
    turns 5-7 only.
- Not yet run: live E1-open on a real GPU (needs Teja to run it on
  Colab or a GPU box; see experiments/e1_open/README.md).

## 2026-11-05 22:45 PST -- commit 874a602
- Live run findings (Colab L4, vLLM 0.33.0, Qwen3-4B, Nov 5-6, 2026):
  agreement 90.0%, Pass NO, only retry_replay failed (0/10). Qwen3-8B
  failed to start on the Colab L4 ("RuntimeError: Engine core
  initialization failed", server never ready in 10 min). vLLM 0.33.0
  also rejected tool-carrying requests with HTTP 400 ("`auto` tool
  choice requires --enable-auto-tool-choice and --tool-call-parser").
- What changed: (1) vllm_server.sh and colab_e1_open.ipynb now start
  vLLM with --enable-auto-tool-choice --tool-call-parser hermes
  (Qwen3 emits Hermes-style tool calls). (2) RETRY_REPLAY no longer
  uses POST /reset_prefix_cache (HTTP 404 on vLLM 0.33.0). Retry
  turns now use a fresh upstream session id (prefixwise_upstream_
  session_id, popped by the proxy before forwarding) plus a fresh
  cache_salt per turn, so the vLLM prefix is cold; the proxy session
  is unchanged, so the classifier still compares against the previous
  turn in the same session. A fresh session_id alone would NOT cold
  the cache: session_id is KV-event metadata, not a cache partition;
  cache_salt is the documented vLLM mechanism (mixed into the first
  block's hash). (3) Colab default is now Qwen/Qwen3-4B; 8B needs a
  larger GPU (RTX 4090 / A100 class). README.md and
  experiments/e1_open/README.md document all three. results/ added
  to .gitignore (run artifacts, not committed).
- Tests: PYTHONPATH=src python3 -m pytest tests/ -q -- 31 passed in
  0.98s (28 existing + 3 new: retry_upstream_ids fresh per turn,
  retry turns carry fresh upstream sessions in mock, proxy pops the
  upstream-session override and forwards it as X-Session-ID).
  pytest was not installed in this VM; installed with pip
  --break-system-packages (local env only, not part of the repo).
- Mock run: PYTHONPATH=src python3 experiments/e1_open/e1_open.py
  --mock -- 100 turns, agreement 100.0%, UNKNOWN rate 0.0%,
  Pass YES, all 9 causes 100% (retry_replay 10/10). Mock only, not
  live evidence: the live re-run on Colab (Qwen3-4B, fixed flags)
  is still needed to confirm retry_replay passes for real.
- Not yet run live: the fixed E1-open on Colab/GPU box.
